{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '200,380p' TOPOPILOT_SCRIPTING_GUIDE.txt && sed -n '190,270p' TopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/nodes/fieldVisualizationNodes.py && sed -n '340,400p' TopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/nodes/pointNodes.py && sed -n '1,260p' TopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/ui/script_template.py\"","aggregated_output":"\n    pvbatch my_pipeline.py -i ./data.vti -t 1 -o output.png\n\nSingle VTI interactively:\n\n    python3 my_pipeline.py -i ./data.vti -t 1 -x\n\nAll steps of a time-series directory to MP4:\n\n    pvbatch my_pipeline.py -i path/to/NAME -t -1 -o output.mp4 -q session\n\nOne time step from a time-series directory to PNG:\n\n    pvbatch my_pipeline.py -i path/to/NAME -t 4 -o output.png -q session\n\nCLI options:\n\n  -i PATH   Required .vti file or time-series directory.\n  -x        Interactive mode; cannot be combined with -o, and cannot display a\n            multi-step input with -t -1.\n  -o PATH   Output .png for one step or .mp4 for all steps.\n  -t N      One-based time step; -1 means all steps (default).\n  -q DIR    Session, cache, and temporary-frame directory (default: current dir).\n\nVideo output requires ffmpeg on PATH. The template currently invokes it at 4 fps.\n\n\n6. NODE REFERENCE\n=================\n\nIn every non-loader constructor, parent_node_id is the id of the immediately\npreceding compatible node. Defaults are shown below.\n\n\nDATA LOADERS (ROOT NODES)\n-------------------------\n\nLoadScalarField(load_path, arrayName=\"\")\n    Loads a scalar field. load_path is a VTI or time-series directory. arrayName is\n    the point-data array; it may be empty only when the file has one array.\n\nLoadVectorField(load_path, u_array_name, v_array_name)\n    Loads a 2D vector field from the point arrays holding its x/u and y/v\n    components.\n\nLoadSymmetricTensorField(load_path, A_array_name, B_array_name, D_array_name)\n    Loads a 2D symmetric tensor [[A, B], [B, D]] from three point arrays.\n\nLoadAsymmetricTensorField(load_path, A_array_name, B_array_name,\n                          C_array_name, D_array_name)\n    Loads a 2D general tensor [[A, B], [C, D]] from four point arrays.\n\n\nFIELD EMBEDDINGS\n----------------\n\nEmbedScalarField(parent_node_id, colormap=\"cool warm\")\n    Displays a scalar field as a colored surface (2D) or volume (3D). colormap must\n    be one of the colormap names listed in Section 2.\n\nEmbedVectorField(parent_node_id)\n    Displays a vector field using its geometric vector-field embedding.\n\nEmbedSymmetricTensorField(parent_node_id)\n    Displays a symmetric tensor field using its geometric tensor embedding.\n\nEmbedAsymmetricTensorFieldEigenvectorPartition(parent_node_id, resolution=16)\n    Displays the asymmetric-tensor domain partitioned by eigenvector behavior.\n    resolution is the number of subdivisions per grid cell; higher is slower and\n    smoother.\n\nEmbedAsymmetricTensorFieldEigenvaluePartition(parent_node_id, resolution=16)\n    Displays regions dominated by scaling, rotation, or anisotropic stretching,\n    including direction where applicable. resolution controls subdivisions per\n    grid cell.\n\n\nSCALAR OPERATIONS AND TOPOLOGICAL STRUCTURES\n--------------------------------------------\n\nPersistenceSimplification(parent_node_id, epsilon)\n    Simplifies a scalar field. epsilon is a fraction of the function range: 0 means\n    no simplification and 1 spans the entire range.\n\nComputePersistenceDiagram(parent_node_id)\n    Computes a scalar field's persistence diagram.\n\nEmbedPersistenceDiagram(parent_node_id, ball_radius=0.02, tube_radius=0.01)\n    Displays persistence pairs as balls and tubes. Both radii are fractions of the\n    scalar function range.\n\nComputeMorseSmaleSegmentation(parent_node_id)\n    Computes the Morse-Smale segmentation of a scalar field.\n\nEmbedMorseSmaleSegmentation(parent_node_id)\n    Creates displayable geometry for a Morse-Smale segmentation.\n\nComputeIsocontours(parent_node_id, num_contours)\n    Computes num_contours isovalues uniformly across a scalar field's value range.\n\nEmbedIsocontours(parent_node_id, colormap=\"cool warm\", tube_radius=1.0)\n    Displays isocontours with the selected colormap. tube_radius is the contour tube\n    radius used for 2D data.\n\nComputeContourTree(parent_node_id)\n    Computes a scalar field's contour tree.\n\nEmbedContourTree(parent_node_id, ball_radius=3.0, tube_radius=1.5,\n                 color_scheme=[\"#002fff\", \"#758fff\", \"#ffdee7\", \"#ff0046\",\n                               \"#000000\"])\n    Displays contour-tree vertices and edges. ball_radius and tube_radius size the\n    geometry. color_scheme must contain five hex colors for minima, 1-saddles,\n    2-saddles, maxima, and degenerate points, in that order.\n\nComputeMergeTree(parent_node_id, which_tree=\"join\")\n    Computes a merge tree. which_tree must be \"join\" or \"split\".\n\nEmbedMergeTree(parent_node_id, ball_radius=3.0, tube_radius=1.5,\n               color_scheme=[\"#002fff\", \"#758fff\", \"#ffdee7\", \"#ff0046\",\n                             \"#000000\"])\n    Displays merge-tree vertices and edges. Parameters have the same meanings and\n    color order as EmbedContourTree.\n\n\nFIELD-TO-FIELD OPERATIONS\n-------------------------\n\nVectorFieldMagnitude(parent_node_id)\n    Converts a vector field to a scalar magnitude field.\n\nSymmetricTensorMagnitude(parent_node_id)\n    Converts a symmetric tensor field to a scalar magnitude field.\n\nAsymmetricTensorMagnitude(parent_node_id)\n    Converts an asymmetric tensor field to a scalar magnitude field.\n\nScalarGradient(parent_node_id)\n    Converts a scalar field to its vector gradient field.\n\nVectorGradient(parent_node_id)\n    Converts a vector field to its asymmetric-tensor gradient/Jacobian field.\n\n\nPOINT COMPUTATION AND EMBEDDING\n-------------------------------\n\nComputeScalarCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, which_points)\n    Computes selected critical points of a scalar field. which_points must be one\n    of these exact strings:\n      - \"all critical points (mins+maxes+saddles)\"\n      - \"minima\"\n      - \"maxima\"\n      - \"saddles\"\n      - \"all contour tree vertices (mins+maxes+saddles)\"\n      - \"contour tree saddles\"\n\nComputeVectorCriticalPoints(parent_node_id)\n    Computes critical points of a vector field.\n\nComputeSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id)\n    Computes degenerate points of a symmetric tensor field.\n\nComputeAsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id)\n    Computes degenerate points of an asymmetric tensor field.\n\nEmbedScalarCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0,\n                          color_scheme=[\"#3b4cc0\", \"#aac7fd\", \"#f7b89c\",\n                                        \"#b40426\", \"#000000\"])\n    Displays scalar critical points as spheres. radius controls sphere size.\n    color_scheme contains five hex colors for minima, index-1 saddles, index-2\n    saddles, maxima, and degenerate points.\n\nEmbedVectorCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0,\n                          color_scheme=[\"#9d2c00\", \"#f0c571\", \"#0b81a2\",\n                                        \"#e25759\", \"#7e4794\", \"#59a89c\"])\n    Displays vector critical points as spheres. The six colors represent sources,\n    saddles, sinks, source spirals, centers, and sink spirals.\n\nEmbedSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0,\n                                     color_scheme=[\"#ffffff\", \"#ff8cc6\"])\n    Displays symmetric-tensor degenerate points. The two colors represent\n                          f\"of type {other.node_type.get_mcp_name()}. They will overlap in the visualization\"\n\n        return True, \"\"\n\n    def _evaluation_logic(self, parent_data, time_step):\n        resolution = 16\n\n        array = paraview_vti_to_numpy(parent_data.data)\n        lic_array = lic(array, 16)\n        data = numpy_to_paraview_vti(lic_array, 16)\n\n        return SurfaceOrVolumeEmbedding(data, \"grey\", None, array.shape)\n\nclass EmbedAsymmetricTensorFieldEigenvectorPartition(Node):\n    def __init__(self, parent_node_id : str, resolution : int = 16):\n        super().__init__(parent_node_id, AsymmetricTensor, EigenvectorPartitionEmbedding, locals())\n\n        self.resolution = resolution\n\n    @classmethod\n    def guardrails(cls):\n        return [\n            Guardrail(\n                get_prompt(\"guardrails\", \"eigenvector_partition_degenerate_points\"),\n                \"degenerate_points_are_also_embedded\",\n                \"Set to True if degenerate points will be separately computed and visualized. Set to False otherwise.\",\n                raise_on_tool_param_false(\n                    \"Cannot create this node because visualizing the eigenvector partition also requires separately \"\n                    \"computing and visualizing the degenerate points.\"\n                ),\n            ),\n            _visualize_alongside_descriptors_guardrail\n        ]\n\n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"queued embedding asymmetric tensor field eigenvector partition\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def description(cls):\n        from topopilot.config import correctness_checks_on\n\n        desc = 'Creates a geometric embedding of a node of type asymmetric_tensor. It will display the ' \\\n               'eigenvector partition. It partitions the domain according to whether rotation or ' \\\n               'anisotropic stretching is stronger as well as the direction of rotation.'\n        \n        if not correctness_checks_on():\n            desc += \"This function does not compute the degenerate points, yet the degenerate points are part of the eigenvector \"\\\n                    \"partition. Thus, when visualizing the eigenvector partition, also separately compute and visualize \"\\\n                    \"the degenerate points using a separate function.\"\n            \n        return desc\n\n    @classmethod\n    def param_descriptions(cls):\n        return {'parent_node_id': 'The id of a node of type asymmetric_tensor that should be '\n                           'embedded.',\n         'resolution': 'How many times should each grid cell be subdivided when displaying the '\n                       'partition. Higher values are more computationally expensive but lead '\n                       'to better visual results.'}\n\n    def compatible_to_visualize(self, other):\n        if issubclass(other.node_type, SquareOrCubeEmbedding):\n            return False, f\"Cannot embed a node of type {self.node_type.get_mcp_name()} along with another \"\\\n                          f\"of type {other.node_type.get_mcp_name()}. They will overlap in the visualization\"\n\n        return True, \"\"\n\n    def _evaluation_logic(self, parent_data, time_step):\n\n        f = servermanager.Fetch(parent_data.data)\n\n        array = paraview_vti_to_numpy(parent_data.data)\n        partition_array = eigenvector_partition(array, self.resolution)\n        dimensions = servermanager.Fetch(parent_data.data).GetDimensions()\n\n        return EigenvectorPartitionEmbedding(numpy_to_paraview_vti(partition_array, self.resolution), dimensions)\n    \nclass EmbedAsymmetricTensorFieldEigenvaluePartition(Node):\n    def __init__(self, parent_node_id : str, resolution : int = 16):\n        super().__init__(parent_node_id, AsymmetricTensor, EigenvaluePartitionEmbedding, locals())\n\n    def _evaluation_logic_partial_cache(self, parent_data, partial_cache, time_step):\n        return _embed_criticalPoints_partial_cache(parent_data, partial_cache)\n\n\nclass EmbedAsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(Node):\n\n    def __init__(self, parent_node_id : str, radius : float = 3.0, color_scheme : List[str] = [\"#ffffff\", \"#ff8cc6\"]):\n        if correctness_checks_on():\n            if len(color_scheme) != 2:\n                raise Exception(\"color_scheme list should have two entries\")\n\n            for elt in color_scheme:\n                if not is_hex_string(elt):\n                    raise Exception(f\"Element {elt} in color_scheme is not a hex string\")\n\n            del elt\n\n        super().__init__(parent_node_id, types.AsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints, types.AsymmetricTensorDegeneratePointsEmbedding, locals(), False, True)\n\n        self.radius = radius\n        self.color_scheme = color_scheme\n\n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"queued embedding asymmetric tensor field degenerate points\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def description(cls):\n        return 'Create a geometric embedding of the degenerate points of asymmetric tensor field data.'\n\n    @classmethod\n    def param_descriptions(cls):\n        return {'parent_node_id': 'A node of type asymmetric_tensor_dp which corresponds to some '\n                           'degenerate points that should be visualized.',\n         'radius': 'The radius of the spheres that will be used to visualize the degenerate '\n                   'points.',\n         'color_scheme': 'A list of two hex strings that respectively correspond to the colors that '\n                   'will be used to visualize trisectors and wedges.'}\n\n    def compatible_to_visualize(self, other):\n        if issubclass(other.node_type, types.TrackedAsymmetricTensorDegeneratePointsEmbedding) and \\\n           self.parent_node_id == other.parent_node.parent_node_id:\n\n            return False, \"Cannot visualize an asymmetric tensor field's set of degenerate points both tracked and \"\\\n                          \"untracked at the same time. They will overlap.\"\n\n        return True, \"\"\n\n    def _evaluation_logic(self, parent_data, time_step):\n        return types.AsymmetricTensorDegeneratePointsEmbedding(parent_data.points, self.radius, \"CriticalType\", color_list_to_lut(self.color_scheme))\n\n    def _evaluation_logic_partial_cache(self, parent_data, partial_cache, time_step):\n        return _embed_criticalPoints_partial_cache(parent_data, partial_cache)\n    \nmodule_summary = ModuleSummary(\"critical and degenerate pionts\",\n                               \"Computation and visualization of scalar field critical points, vector field critical \"\n                               \"points, and tensor field degenerate points\")\nfrom paraview.simple import *\nfrom topopilot.nodes import *\nimport topopilot.config as config\nimport topopilot.nodeTree as tree\nimport argparse\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nDEFAULT_RANDOM_SEED = 0\n\ndef pipeline(load_path):\n    pass\n\ndef create_view():\n    pass\n\ndef validate_arguments(args):\n    if args.i[-4:] == \".vti\":\n        time_steps = 1\n    else:\n        if not os.path.isdir(args.i):\n            print(\"error: file specified with -i must either be .vti file or directory\")\n            exit(1)\n        \n        time_steps = len(os.listdir(args.i))\n        \n        basename = os.path.basename(args.i)\n        dirname = os.path.dirname(args.i)\n\n        for i in range(1,time_steps+1):\n            \n            if not os.path.isfile(f\"{dirname}/{basename}/{basename}{i}.vti\"):\n                print(\"error: invalid input format for directory\")\n                print(f\"missing file {dirname}/{basename}/{basename}{i}.vti\")\n                exit(1)\n        \n    if args.t > time_steps:\n        print(\"error: time step is too high\")\n        exit(1)                             \n\n    if args.x and args.t == -1 and time_steps > 1:\n        print(\"error: cannot run interactive mode on multiple time steps\")\n        exit(1)\n                                    \n    if args.o != \"\" and args.x:\n        print(\"error: you cannot specify an output file and -interactive\")\n        exit(1)\n    \n    if args.o == \"\" and not args.x:\n        print(\"error: you must either specify an output file or run in interactive mode.\")\n        exit(1)\n                                    \n    if args.t == -1 and time_steps > 1 and args.o[-4:] != \".mp4\":\n        print(\"error: when outputting to video format your output filename must end in .mp4\")\n        exit(1)\n    \n    if args.t != -1 and not args.x and args.o[-4:] != \".png\":\n        print(\"error: when outputting to image format your output filename must end in .png\")\n        exit(1)\n                                    \n    if args.t == -1 and time_steps == 1:\n        args.t = 1\n\n    return time_steps\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"User generated scientific visualization pipeline. Generates images or videos based on user input.\")\n\n    parser.add_argument(\"-i\", help=\"The file that should be loaded.\", required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"-x\", help=\"Should you load into interactive mode? (no images will be generated)\", action=argparse.BooleanOptionalAction)\n    parser.add_argument(\"-o\", help=\"The name of the file that we are outputting.\", default=\"\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"-t\", help=\"What time step should be loaded. Put -1 to generate a video of all time steps. If the data only has one time step, -1 will just load the one time step.\", type=int, default=-1)\n    parser.add_argument(\"-q\", help=\"What folder should be used for temporary files\", default=\".\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--seed\", help=\"Seed for TopoPilot-owned random colors and identifiers.\", type=int, default=DEFAULT_RANDOM_SEED)\n\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    time_steps = validate_arguments(args)\n\n    config.set_random_seed(args.seed)\n    config.change_session_folder(args.q)\n\n    sessionDir = Path(f\"{config.session_folder()}\")\n    sessionDir.mkdir(exist_ok = True)\n    cacheDir = Path(f\"{config.session_folder()}/cache\")\n    cacheDir.mkdir(exist_ok = True)\n\n    nodes_to_visualize, color_bar_info, time_invariant_nodes_to_cache, normal_nodoes_to_cache = pipeline(args.i)\n\n    if args.t != -1:\n\n        renderView = create_view()\n        renderView.Background = [1.0, 1.0, 1.0]\n        renderView.UseColorPaletteForBackground = 0\n\n        for n in nodes_to_visualize:\n            props = n.visualize(args.t, renderView)\n\n            if n.id in color_bar_info:\n                position, length, title = color_bar_info[n.id]\n\n                lut = props.LookupTable\n                bar = GetScalarBar(lut, renderView)\n\n                bar.WindowLocation = \"Any Location\"\n                bar.Position = position\n                bar.ScalarBarLength = length\n                bar.Title = title\n                bar.ComponentTitle = ''\n\n                props.SetScalarBarVisibility(renderView, True)\n\n        if args.o:\n            SaveScreenshot(args.o)\n        else:\n            Interact()\n\n    else:\n\n        for t in range(time_steps):\n\n            renderView = create_view()\n\n            for n in nodes_to_visualize:\n                props = n.visualize(t+1, renderView)\n\n                if n.id in color_bar_info:\n                    position, length, title = color_bar_info[n.id]\n\n                    lut = props.LookupTable\n                    bar = GetScalarBar(lut, renderView)\n\n                    bar.WindowLocation = \"Any Location\"\n                    bar.Position = position\n                    bar.ScalarBarLength = length\n                    bar.Title = title\n                    bar.ComponentTitle = ''\n\n                    props.SetScalarBarVisibility(renderView, True)\n\n            SaveScreenshot(f\"{args.q}/frame{str(t+1).zfill(8)}.png\", renderView)\n\n            Disconnect()\n            tree.clear_evaluation_cache()\n            Connect()\n\n        os.system(f\"ffmpeg -framerate 4 -i {args.q}/frame%08d.png -c:v libx264 -pix_fmt yuv420p {args.o}\")\n\n        for t in range(time_steps):\n            os.remove(f\"{args.q}/frame{str(t+1).zfill(8)}.png\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
